{"availability":"available","full":"RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses","name":"best-of-Agent-Harnesses","description":"🏆 Ranked list of 167 AI agent harnesses, plus templates, playbooks, MCP, and learning resources. Rescored weekly.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1058,"forks":59,"created":"2026-03-07T22:55:23Z","updated":"2026-10-03T14:14:37Z","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ryanalberts.github.io/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/","topics":["agent-framework","agent-harness","agentic-ai","agents","ai-agent","ai-agent-framework","ai-agents","ai-tools","awesome-list","best-of-list","claude-code","coding-agents","harness","harness-engineering","llm","llm-agents","llm-framework","llm-tools","mcp","model-context-protocol"],"demo":null,"color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.924Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.924Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.924Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:14:58.842Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:33.360Z","stars":1056,"forks":59},{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.924Z","stars":1058,"forks":59}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A model answers; an agent acts. An agent harness is the runtime that turns one into the other: the model thinks, the harness decides what that thinking is allowed to touch.","Simon Willison's definition of the agent itself is the cleanest: \"an LLM agent runs tools in a loop to achieve a goal.\" The harness is everything around that loop: which tools exist, what needs approval, what the model sees each turn, what survives a crash. Andrej Karpathy named the architecture back in 2023: the model is \"the kernel process of a new Operating System\", and the harness is the rest of that OS, its scheduler, permissions, and memory. The SWE-agent paper proved the stakes by coining the agent-computer interface: how tools and feedback are presented changes what a model can do,…","Better models make harnesses more important: more capabilities mean more failure modes, and production needs retry logic, fallbacks, and validation. Harness quality, not just model quality, determines whether agents actually ship. This list ranks projects by relevance to harness concerns (environment, orchestration, lifecycle, guardrails) and by stars/activity."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"922a6e0d5d3b3ee32379114bb3b253f34dd73a8b721193a9e5a909a75202eb08","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:14:58.815Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A model answers; an agent acts. An agent harness is the runtime that turns one into the other: the model thinks, the harness decides what that thinking is allowed to touch.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Always-on, self-hosted agents you run as a daemon and talk to from chat apps: gateway runtimes, second brains, and self-improving assistants.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"922a6e0d5d3b3ee32379114bb3b253f34dd73a8b721193a9e5a909a75202eb08","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:14:58.816Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T14:14:37Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:23.476Z","latestRelease":{"name":"Mid-September 2026: the harness-matters-more catalog, QM, Prime Agent, OpenJarvis","tag":"list-2026-09-2","publishedAt":"2026-09-14T17:28:02Z","url":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent-Harnesses/releases/tag/list-2026-09-2"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:23.476Z","screenshots":[],"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RyanAlberts/best-of-Agent